<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osorkon III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 787–759 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osorkon III was a king of the Twenty-third Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, a Libyan line that ruled parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-egypt">Upper Egypt</a> alongside the Bubastite kings. He ruled as co-regent with his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takelot-iii">Takelot III</a> and placed his family as high priests of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amun">Amun</a> and as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gods-wife-of-amun">God's Wife of Amun</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a>, a post held by his daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shepenupet-i">Shepenupet I</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osorkon-iii.jpg" alt="Osorkon III" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: VivaFox · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Limestone_statue_of_Osorkon_III.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
